{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795222,"nonce":"1ydpA6wW+LUCWNiXjkZmiuRjxaQ=","title":"Share Jam build results, playtest artifacts and authorized run actions","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P2\n\nScope\nConnect existing Haxe/Rayzor build/run tasks to explicit source checkpoint IDs and selected shareable results: build state, diagnostics, sanitized output, artifact hashes and download/playtest links. Start with host-local execution and explicit permission for remote requests. Specify cancellation, artifact retention and safe failure behavior. Do not add a remote shell or execute received code merely by joining or following someone.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nA collaborator can correlate a build/artifact with the source that produced it and see failure/stop without blocking UI. Invalid permissions, secret-bearing logs, stale source, failed uploads and interrupted builds do not run unintended commands or overwrite work. Existing non-Jam Build/Run behavior passes its relevant checks.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}